  "label": "The text claims transgender identity is a mental illness, mapped onto the authoritative figure",
  "description": "The textual material 'what if i told you transgender is actually a mental illness called delusional psychosis' is juxtaposed with the visual of a stern, authoritative man. This creates an analogical mapping where the man (visual entity) is implicitly mapped as the 'authority' or 'source' of the harmful claim, reinforcing the stereotype that such claims come from an authoritative, judgmental figure. The man's visual presence serves as a visual anchor for the text's assertion, implying that the claim is presented as fact or truth by an authoritative voice.",
